GeoID Base Data License
=======================

PROVISIONAL — FAO TO CONFIRM (required at milestone 2, not for the June 24 demo).

The GeoID *base dataset* (the geospatial places and their geoids served by this
service) is intended to be released under the:

    Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0
    https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

Rationale: ODbL's share-alike obligation keeps the federated dataset open as
country instances and partners build on it — a Digital Public Good requirement.
(ODC-By is the lighter-weight alternative under consideration; FAO to decide.)

This is distinct from the *service code*, which is licensed under Apache-2.0
(see LICENSE).

Until FAO confirms, treat the base data license as UNSETTLED. Do not assert a
specific data license to donors or partners without that confirmation.

The full, canonical license text will be vendored into this file once confirmed.
